  "notes": "Complex medium: chemically-defined portion mapped to BiGG; biological extracts listed in `unmapped`. Added via GrowthDB curation.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (complete recipe; cited + supplementary sources chased)",
  "verification_evidence": "For broth culture, M. smegmatis was grown on Hartmans de Bont minimal medium [67] supplemented with 0.05% (w/v) tyloxapol and 5.8 mM glycerol.",
  "verification_confidence": "low",
  "base_medium": "Hartmans & de Bont (HdB) mineral (minimal) medium",
  "recuration": {
   "date": "2026-07-16",
   "round": "complete-recipe (cited+supplementary chased)",
   "status": "corrected",
   "confidence": "high",
   "sources_chased": [
    {
     "what": "base recipe cited as ref 67 (Hartmans S, De Bont JAM 1992, Appl Environ Microbiol 58:1220-6, PMID 1599242, PMC195578)",
     "obtained": true,
     "how": "primary is a scanned PDF (PMC195578, text not machine-readable); identical HdB recipe recovered verbatim from Frontiers 2020 (doi:10.3389/fbioe.2020.593781) and corroborated by web search of the primary",
     "added": [
      "(NH4)2SO4 2 g/L",
      "MgCl2 6H2O 0.1 g/L",
      "Na2HPO4 3 g/L",
      "KH2PO4 1 g/L",
      "trace solution: EDTA, ZnSO4, CaCl2, FeSO4, Na2MoO4 (molybdenum), CuSO4, CoCl2, MnCl2"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "missing_before": [
    "molybdenum / molybdate (Na2MoO4) - present in HdB trace solution but absent from current_components (no EX_mobd/EX_mo)",
    "EDTA (chelator in trace solution)",
    "explicit salt identities and concentrations for (NH4)2SO4, MgCl2, Na2HPO4, KH2PO4 and each trace metal (previously only listed as ion exchanges with no source-backed concentrations)",
    "tyloxapol and glycerol previously in current_uncovered / unquantified"
   ],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "HdB is a purely mineral (vitamin-free) medium; mycobacteria need no added vitamins, so none are absent. Trace-element concentrations are the stock values (per Frontiers restatement of Hartmans & de Bont); the stock is added at 10 mL/L, so concentration_mM is the final in-medium molar (100-fold dilution). Only real gap versus current_components is molybdate; Ni/Se/W/B are genuinely not in this recipe. Growth was aerobic (37 C, 200 rpm) despite target 'facultative' tag."
  },
